contract:
FR-28 (amended 4ec6772): "Starting a demo game never ends a player game in progress, and starting a player game never ends a demo game; each only ends games of its own kind."
NFR-14: games in progress survive a restart.
Where: apps/server/src/games.ts create() (around lines 1196-1210):
  const source = opts.source ?? "player";
  const g = newGameRecord(newId(), playerColor, now(), source);
  save(g, { required: true });
  for (const other of games.values()) if (other.status === "playing") abandon(other);
The fix is to filter by other.source === source. g.source comes from #64 (schema v3, stored column source, hydrated at games.ts:524).
Check every other place in apps/server that assumes one playing game, and fix or prove each with a test: startup restore (store.listPlaying() at games.ts:1181 must restore both a playing demo game and a playing player game), the shutdown log count (games.ts:1327, fine as a count), and anything else you find. The engine is shared and runs one search at a time, queued (IR-3): two games' bot moves and analyses just queue; a test that both games get their bot move when both are waiting is enough.
Web: apps/web does not pick a "current game" at / (controller.navigate shows no game when the path has no id; a game is opened by /games/:id), so no web change is needed. Do not touch apps/web.
Store: no schema change expected. If you think one is needed, stop and report it as a contract_gap instead.
Helpers: apps/server/test/helpers.ts. Existing homes: games-api.test.ts (routes, incl. the demo token from #64), game-survival.test.ts (restarts).
